# A0c: the NON-INTERLEAVED CONTROL of the exactness pair, on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-control-audit (the audited best arm plus QWEN_FAST_LEVERN_AUDIT=1 alone: chunked prefill off, the whole-prompt path, the digest instrument on).
# Tests: warmup, one coding stream, levern_equal (one user alone: prompts of exactly 2,047 / 2,048 / 2,049 / 4,095 / 4,096 / 4,097 / 6,143 / 6,145 / 32,785 tokens, 256 out), levern_equal_busy (seven seats
# decoding while 4,097 / 6,145 / 32,785 arrive) and levern_equal_long (131,077 and 253,920). READ: admission passed at capacity 262144, every answer completes, c2_smoke_check clean (a digest line for every prompt of
# every levern_equal test: "[PINDIAG] lever N digest"), no stall. This run is A1's REFERENCE: record its smoke log and container log for levern_compare.py. Duration (estimate): 2.5 h (the KV digests read the whole pool to the host, about a minute each). Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/lever-n four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/lever-n and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/lever-n commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-lever-n-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-levern-control-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,levern_equal,levern_equal_busy,levern_equal_long
